	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the title is printed as 12-4 2-4/Duplicities. The page marks the start Open Feel (dotted quarter = 60) and the B part Latin.
	- the real book handwriting has many dotted eighths against the 6/8 beat. The rest in the first bar of lines 1 and 2 is typed as a dotted eighth rest (it looks like a dotted quarter rest, which does not fit the bar).
	- bar 5 (Abmaj7): the first note is read as an A flat on the first ledger line above the staff, the Bb edition seems to read it differently, check it.
	- bar 12: the a flat is printed as a dotted half note, which does not fit the bar with the two sixteenth triplets after it, typed as a dotted quarter tied to an eighth.
	- the B flat vamp at the end of the B part: its second and third bars have only rhythm figures for the band (repeat signs) and no melody, they are rests here.
	- the parenthesized pickup at the end of the vamp is hard to read, check it.
	- the band rhythm figures under the vamp and under the Latin bars of the solos are not typed in.
	- the two bars of the solos with diamond note heads (A-7, Ab lydian) are typed as plain b notes, check them against the Bb edition (which reads them a tone lower).
	- the solos end with D.C. al Fine; the Ending only bar is the Fine.
